Subject: [PATCH] Throttle blip on downshift with the electronic throttle,
 outra-ecu style

Plan item 59 (from the outra-ecu T20K manual; pulled forward from phase 4,
item 52, because it is useful on the street too).
- new module DownshiftBlip: each press of the blip button (or a micro
  switch on the clutch or the gear lever) adds blipThrottleAdd % to the
  throttle target for blipDuration ms, only at or above blipMinRpm;
  holding the button does not make the blip longer
- added on top of the pedal target, before the throttle maximum position
  and the throttle rev limiter
- 0 % = off (default)
- output channel / log: Downshift blip throttle add
- TunerStudio: Throttle blip on downshift (electronic throttle menu)
- 4 new tests

